{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de21f67e39d99b57bc5b5e", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "Thermodynamics (C) - Test 5", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 30, "totalQuestions": 20, "totalMarks": 80, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d91", "totalMarks": 80, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 20, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d929778e"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d929778b", "title": "Chemistry Numerical", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d91", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d9297710", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476e"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f1a"], "question": {"text": "For combustion of one mole of magnesium in an open container at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;bar pressure, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></msub><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>&#8854;</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>601</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>70</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>, the magnitude of change in internal energy for the reaction is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>kJ</mi></math>. (Nearest integer)<br />(Given : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>)"}, "options": [{"id": "57e44b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d9297711"}, {"id": "81b9b0", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d9297712"}, {"id": "6d78c5", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d9297713"}, {"id": "54852c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d9297714"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d9297715", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4783"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e51"], "question": {"text": "The reaction of cyanamide, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>CN</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced></msub></math> with oxygen was run in a bomb calorimeter and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;U</mi></math> was found to be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>742</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>24</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> . The magnitude of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#916;H</mi><mn>298</mn></msub></math> for the reaction&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>CN</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced></mrow></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mfenced></msub></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>kJ</mi></math>. (Rounded off to the nearest integer) [Assume ideal gases and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>314</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>]"}, "options": [{"id": "63f6d0", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d9297716"}, {"id": "e8563f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d9297717"}, {"id": "8e1ad4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d9297718"}, {"id": "408be1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d9297719"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d929771a", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e5671c499d1e49588f8808"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b61"], "question": {"text": "<p>For a dimerization reaction,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>298</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#916;</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">U</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>20</mn><msup><mi>kJmol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>&#916;</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>30</mn><msup><mi>JK</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>,then the&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;will be &hellip;..J.</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "bc925c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d929771b"}, {"id": "0b4ac7", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d929771c"}, {"id": "28fefb", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d929771d"}, {"id": "a79d49", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d929771e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d929771f", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476e"], "concepts": ["6117b90767dbe2603c3e8fd4"], "question": {"text": "<p>One mole of an ideal monoatomic gas is subjected to changes as shown in the graph. The magnitude of the work done (by the system or on the system) is _______ J (nearest integer)</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fdc0a0793-33aa-4873-8287-d48ce7fa0823-9894345.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 275px;\" /><br /><br />Given : log 2 = 0.3, ln 10 = 2.3</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "83e78c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d9297720"}, {"id": "af0db8", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d9297721"}, {"id": "81026f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d9297722"}, {"id": "105c61", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d9297723"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d9297724", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e5671c499d1e49588f8808"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b65"], "question": {"text": "For a certain thermochemical reaction <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>400</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ΔH</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>77</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo> </mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><msup><mi>ΔS</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>122</mn><msup><mi>JK</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>log</mi></math> equilibrium constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>logK</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo></math> _____<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>."}, "options": [{"id": "b519c3", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d9297725"}, {"id": "1abe77", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d9297726"}, {"id": "38a977", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d9297727"}, {"id": "700179", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d9297728"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d9297729", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4783"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b473a"], "question": {"text": "Consider the following data :\nHeat of formation of $\\mathrm{CO}_2(\\mathrm{~g})=-393.5 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$\nHeat of formation of $\\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O}(\\mathrm{l})=-286.0 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$\nHeat of combustion of benzene $=-3267.0 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$\nThe heat of formation of benzene is _ $\\mathrm{kJ} \\mathrm{mol}{ }^{-1}$. (Nearest integer)"}, "options": [{"id": "d9c067", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d929772a"}, {"id": "2cf062", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d929772b"}, {"id": "6a03d3", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d929772c"}, {"id": "2bafd2", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d929772d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d929772e", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476e"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4725"], "question": {"text": "An ideal gas, \\(\\overline{\\mathrm{C}}_{\\mathrm{v}}=\\frac{5}{2} \\mathrm{R}\\), is expanded adiabatically against a constant pressure of 1 atm untill it doubles in volume. If the initial temperature and pressure is \\(298 \\mathrm{~K}\\) and \\(5 \\mathrm{~atm}\\), respectively then the final temperature is _______ \\(\\mathrm{K}\\) (nearest integer).\n[\\(\\overline{\\mathrm{C}}_{\\mathrm{v}}\\) is the molar heat capacity at constant volume]"}, "options": [{"id": "e22300", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d929772f"}, {"id": "b54374", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d9297730"}, {"id": "7df4b0", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d9297731"}, {"id": "d888b9", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d9297732"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d9297733", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4783"], "concepts": ["60e567dc499d1e49588f9cb8"], "question": {"text": "For the reaction<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math><br />the reaction enthalpy <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>in</mi></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>kJmol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<br />(Round off to the Nearest Integer).<br />[Given : Bond enthalpies in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>kJmol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>:</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>:</mo></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>347</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>:</mo><mn>611</mn><mo>;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>:</mo><mn>414</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>:</mo><mn>436</mn><mo>]</mo></math>"}, "options": [{"id": "55f7f2", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d9297734"}, {"id": "5836ff", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d9297735"}, {"id": "bb1edb", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d9297736"}, {"id": "d3f324", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d9297737"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d9297738", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e5671c499d1e49588f8808"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b61"], "question": {"text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HI</mi></math> undergoes decomposition to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>.</mo><msup><mi>&#916;G</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#920;</mi></msup></math> for this decompostion reaction at one atmopsphere pressure is____<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Jmol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>-[nearest integer]</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>Use</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>31</mn><msup><mi>JK</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>;</mo><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3010</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>ln</mi><mn>10</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>log</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>477</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "1dfd0d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d9297739"}, {"id": "f880ec", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d929773a"}, {"id": "a6f0e0", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d929773b"}, {"id": "783db8", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d929773c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d929773d", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476e"], "concepts": ["6162fb896ed13040ec850101"], "question": {"text": "When a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math> electric heater is immersed in a gas for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> in a constant volume container with adiabatic walls, the temperature of the gas rises by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>. The heat capacity of the given gas is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>JK</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> (Nearest integer)"}, "options": [{"id": "a6ca9a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d929773e"}, {"id": "634309", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d929773f"}, {"id": "0b430c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d9297740"}, {"id": "4751b0", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d9297741"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d9297742", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4783"], "concepts": ["6176f3ee6581241c7072a758"], "question": {"text": "<p>The Born-Haber cycle for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>KCl</mi></math> is evaluated with the following data:<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#920;</mi></msup><mtext>&#160;for&#160;</mtext><mi>KCl</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>436.7</mn><msup><mi>kJmol</mi><mrow><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mi>sub</mi></msub><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#920;</mi></msup><mtext>&#160;for&#160;</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>89.2</mn><msup>