": "69de4f882ee0e063d9297763"}, {"id": "1956c6", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d9297764"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d9297765", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e5671c499d1e49588f8808"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b65"], "question": {"text": "<p>Consider the following reaction approaching equilibrium at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>27</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math> atm pressure</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><munder><mover><mo>&#8652;</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>0</mn><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mover><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></munder><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math></p><p>The standard Gibb&#39;s energy change <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow></mfenced></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>27</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mo>-</mo></mfenced></math>&nbsp;_____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>kJmol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;(Nearest integer).</p><p>(Given : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ln</mi><mn>10</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn></math>)</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "697fc5", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d9297766"}, {"id": "20ceb4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d9297767"}, {"id": "193666", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d9297768"}, {"id": "c986e7", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d9297769"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d929776a", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476e"], "concepts": ["6162fb896ed13040ec850107"], "question": {"text": "Five moles of an ideal gas at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>293</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> is expanded isothermally from an initial pressure of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>MPa</mi></math>&nbsp;to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>MPa</mi></math>&nbsp;against at constant external pressure <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>MPa</mi></math>. The heat transferred in this process is ___&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>kJmol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. (Rounded-off to the nearest integer)<p>[ Use <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>314</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>]</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "b31f61", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d929776b"}, {"id": "cc2ec6", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d929776c"}, {"id": "94eed4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d929776d"}, {"id": "507193", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d929776e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d929776f", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8c"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4783"], "concepts": ["6228bb8f5339ae4f88133302"], "question": {"text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of ethane undergoes combustion at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>27</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> in a bomb calorimeter. The temperature of calorimeter system (including the water) is found to rise by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>. The heat evolved during combustion of ethane at constant pressure is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>kJmol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>.<br />(Nearest integer)</p><p>[Given : The heat capacity of the calorimeter system is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>JK</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>.<br />Assume ideal gas behaviour.</p><p>Assume ideal gas behaviour.</p><p>Atomic mass of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> respectively]</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "cb046c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d9297770"}, {"id": "e5c64e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d9297771"}, {"id": "d9b675", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d9297772"}, {"id": "1fb402", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d9297773"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283c623cf4b3ad8f125e5", "title": "JEE Numerical", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:27.056Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 20, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:30:32.237Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:30:32.237Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 0, "_id": "69de4f882ee0e063d929778d"}], "bonusSections": [], "packDetails": [], "paidFeatures": [], "tags": [], "timeRestrictionSlots": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T11:16:06.326Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-17T04:58:03.834Z", "testType": "PYQs as Chapter Tests", "isResumeBufferAllowed": true, "enableAccessibility": true, "maxAttemptableQuestion": 20, "analysisVideoThumbnail": "", "analysisVideoThumbnailDark": "", "shortTitle": "", "subjectDetails": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d91", "title": "Chemistry", "shortName": "Chem"}], "testTimerType": "mm", "isMarkForReviewAvailable": true}, "temporaryTestDetail": {"_id": "6a4a1ec49cbf3c65130567c5", "testId": "69de21f67e39d99b57bc5b5e", "userId": "6914cc9c4d7566258ee3a8fd", "startedAt": "2026-07-05T09:07:16.013Z", "lastAttemptedSection": null, "totalTimeLeft": 30, "bonusAttempt": false, "sections": [{"sectionId": "6